## Using assert

```xiom
fn binary_search(arr: &Vec[Int], target: Int) -> Option[Int]
  requires: is_sorted(arr);
{
  assert(arr.len() > 0);  // Internal: loop assumes non-empty
  var lo = 0;
  var hi = arr.len() - 1;
  while lo <= hi {
    let mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
    assert(mid >= lo && mid <= hi);  // Sanity: mid stays in range
    if arr[mid] == target { return Some(mid); }
    if arr[mid] < target { lo = mid + 1; }
    else { hi = mid - 1; }
  }
  return None();
}
```

### assert vs requires

| Feature | requires | assert |
|---------|----------|--------|
| Location | Function signature | Function body |
| Visibility | Public API | Internal only |
| Strippable | --no-contracts | --no-asserts |
| Purpose | Caller obligations | Developer assumptions |

### assert in Loops

```xiom
fn process(items: &Vec[Int]) -> Int {
  var count = 0;
  for item in items {
    count = count + 1;
    assert(count <= items.len());  // Can never exceed
  }
  assert(count == items.len());    // Should be equal at end
  return count;
}
```

### Conditional Compilation
```xiom
// assert is active in debug, stripped in release (--no-asserts)
assert(x > 0);

// Use @llvm.trap for always-on assertions
if x <= 0 { @llvm.trap(); }
```

